  "articleBody": "When you're upgrading your hallway lighting, it's easy to make a few common blunders that can leave your space feeling underlit or just plain awkward. One frequent mistake is underlighting long hallways. You need to make sure you have enough fixtures spaced appropriately to eliminate dark spots and provide consistent illumination. Another common issue is choosing fixtures that are too large or hang too low for your ceiling height, making the hallway feel cramped or creating a head-bumping hazard! Skipping code checks is another big no-no, especially if you're adding new wiring or circuits. Local codes are there for your safety! And, of course, attempting hardwired installation without proper electrical experience can be dangerous. Always shut off the power at the breaker, verify it's off, and if you're not confident, call in a pro. Avoiding these mistakes will lead to a much safer and better-lit hallway.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
